1785727487722593	console-w-3vg	itc:v3:AWLMkkyZzJPJOZEAAAAAQdqrW7V6u0AAAAEzAw		item.comment	bn-3vg	{"body":"Done in ws bn-3vg (commit b799f41), ready to merge.\n\nDESIGN\n- fillp: two-colour form IMPLEMENTED, not punted. Shape colour args are now c0 + c1*16 (gfx::pat_col masks 0xff instead of 0xf). Clear bit -> low nibble, set bit -> high nibble, or a hole when the high nibble is 0. Both nibbles go through pal(). Solid pattern never reads the high nibble, so old carts passing c>=16 are unchanged. Consequence documented: 'secondary = colour 0, opaque' has no encoding — invert the pattern and swap the colours. Bit 15 = top-left, row-major; grid anchored to SCREEN space (x&3, y&3 after camera). Applies to pset/line/rect/rectfill/circ/circfill only; cls/spr/sspr/map/print exempt. pal() does NOT reset it.\n- sspr: u32.16 fixed point, step = (sw << 16) / dw, all range maths in i64 (j*step provably < sh<<16, no overflow). Loop bounds are pre-clamped to the clip rect, so no per-pixel clip test and no allocation. dw/dh default to sw/sh. Identity scale is byte-identical to spr under every draw-state/flip variant (test pins this). Sizes <= 0 draw nothing, negatives do not mirror.\n- mosaic: applied in Console::sync_framebuffer — after _draw, before the frame is presented — to the SNAPSHOT, from the pristine draw buffer. So it is in framebuffer()/screen_text/screenshots/goldens (contrast: display palette is scanout-only), while pget and the next frame's drawing stay full-res and the effect never compounds. Top-left pixel per f x f block, blocks anchored at screen (0,0), f clamped 1..=32 (MAX_MOSAIC).\n\nFILES\ncrates/console-core/src/gfx.rs (Fill struct, DrawState fillp/mosaic, put/hline/vline take a Fill, sspr, apply_mosaic, pat_col), src/api.rs (surgical: pat_col on the six shape fns, new fillp/mosaic/sspr bindings), src/lib.rs (sync_framebuffer applies mosaic; exports MAX_MOSAIC + FILLP_SIZE), tests/effects.rs (new, 35 tests), SPEC.md (API table rows, draw-state bullets, new 'Frame pipeline' section, host surfaces), skills/build-cart/SKILL.md (draw list + 'Effects worth reaching for' tips), README.md (one line). carts/ and audio.rs untouched.\n\nTESTS: cargo test --workspace green from the workspace (21 suites ok, 0 failed). clippy --all-targets clean. rustfmt clean on the files I touched (pre-existing fmt drift elsewhere left alone). Back-compat verified end to end: trunk console-agent vs workspace console-agent on carts/demo.cart --frames 120 with the standard input script produce bit-identical screen_text.\n\nINTEGRATION: web/engine.js needs a rebuild for the browser shell to get fillp/sspr/mosaic (no host-side code change needed — mosaic is already folded into Console::framebuffer())."}	blake3:K0GeZJJ5OOqcoqhObl9L9tPL4DQeOcwz_wYBOHauTSk
