1785729637409945	console-w-1tv	itc:v3:AWKSZJMnJ8k5OZEAAAAAQatVrr6uu0AAAAEzAw		item.comment	bn-1tv	{"body":"2-op FM landed in .maw/workspaces/bn-1tv (commit 577c6a0). cargo test --workspace green (490 tests), clippy clean.\n\nMODEL: carrier phase-modulated by one modulator, both sine. Const quarter-wave sine table SINE_QUARTER: 257 f32 literals = sin(2*pi*k/1024) for k=0..256, generated at authoring time and pasted in like NOTE_FREQ. Quarter + reflection (not a full cycle) so the symmetries are BIT-exact: zeros land on 0.0, peaks on +/-1.0, sine(-p) == -sine(p) and sine(p + half turn) == -sine(p) to the last bit (unit-tested). Linear interpolation over a 16-bit fraction of the 32-bit phase, written a*(1-f)+b*f in every quadrant so the sign flips stay exact. Interp error ~1.2e-6 (-118 dBFS).\n\nRATIO ENCODING: 0.5-15.0 in steps of 0.5, written as a musician writes it (0.5, 1, 2, 3.5, 7; 2.0 accepted). Stored as an integer count of HALVES (ratio_half 1..30), so mod_inc = (inc as u64 * ratio_half) >> 1 -- exact, no rounding to specify. Halves because the chips work that way (YM2612 MUL = 0.5 then 1-15) and because the half-integers are precisely the inharmonic/bell case worth having. Modulator increment is recomputed from the carrier's EVERY SAMPLE (not cached), which is what makes vib/sweep/sl/arp bend both operators and hold the ratio -- pinned by a_pitch_bend_moves_both_operators_together.\n\nINDEX: 0-15, one step = 2^29 phase units = 1/8 cycle peak deviation (beta ~= 0.785*index rad). index=0 is an exact pure sine (the console's first clean one). DECAY: 0-15, per-frame multiply by a const 0.5^(1/half-life) table (half-lives 120,90,64,48,36,27,20,15,11,8,6,4,3,2,1 frames), decaying toward 0, snapped to 0 below 1/1024, re-armed on every note-on. Separate from env by design.\n\nSYNTAX/ERRORS (all parse-time, no silent fallback): wave=6 requires fm=; fm= on any other wave is an error; a bare 6 in a sfx row's wave column is an error with a bespoke message pointing at the inst syntax (a digit carries no parameters). Ratio off the 0.5 grid or outside range, index/decay >15 all error. Wave id 7 still reserved and rejected.\n\nGOLDENS: all five existing hashes UNCHANGED and re-verified (DEMO 0xbc2bd5e1f8c7f31e, GROOVE 0x993ee5118be1bec4, AB 0xba780b637bd94ac3, ECHO 0x7a66500c06d8d557, WAVETABLE 0xf8c700f2fd628f7b). New SOUNDTEST_FM_GOLDEN = 0xff453c589449e0ae (entry 16, pattern 15, 150 played frames).\n\nSOUNDTEST: one appended entry 'FM  2-OP' (17th). 17 rows did NOT fit at top=20 -- the last row's highlight band ended at 154 and the meter starts at 148. Minimal relayout: top 20->18, meter 148->155, banner 168->173, description block 176..205 -> 181..210. Status lines untouched. Screenshotted at 2x with the entry both unselected and playing: everything fits, no overlap, bottom ends at 250 of 256. Entry is Am-F-C-G, 2 bars: fm_bass 1,10,13 on ch0 (eighth notes), fm_epian 3.5,6,7 on ch1 (comping, uses sl and arp), fm_bell 7,11,2 on ch2. NOTE the bell channel is speed=64 x 4 rows, not speed=auto x 32 -- rests are silence on this console, so a bell can only ring across a chord if the ROW is that long. Without that the entry dropped into full silence twice a bar; measured and fixed. audio_stats: peak 0.61, 0 clipped, no window below 0.025 rms.\n\nFILES: crates/console-core/src/audio.rs (FM section + Fm struct + parser + Channel state), crates/console-core/src/lib.rs (re-exports: Fm, WAVE_FM, SINE_QUARTER, FM_DECAY_HALF_LIFE, MIN/MAX_FM_RATIO_HALF, MAX_FM_INDEX, MAX_FM_DECAY), crates/console-core/tests/audio.rs (+14 tests, 4 error-message assertions updated for the widened wave range), carts/soundtest.cart, SPEC.md (new '2-op FM (phase 1.9)' section + waveform list + instruments syntax + wavetable reserved-id note + soundtest blurb), skills/build-cart/SKILL.md (syntax + a 5-patch copy-paste recipe box, all five verified to parse and render clean). Did NOT touch gfx.rs, cart.rs, or any host crate -- console-agent passes wave ids through as u8, so audio_state/audio_events report an FM voice as wave 6 with no change.\n\nINTEGRATION: web/engine.js needs a rebuild and dist needs a repack before an FM cart plays in the browser. web/smoke.cjs's AUDIO_GOLDEN is unchanged (still 0xbc2bd5e1f8c7f31e), so the committed engine is not WRONG -- it just cannot render wave 6 yet."}	blake3:n_ElHfzXiPKYuWCBhggrq6EkmJXtGYCsB75j8SRt75E
