1785729770774818	console-w-qw3	itc:v3:AWLM8yZ-TPM9AAAAAAAAQdva363t4AAAAAErAw		item.comment	bn-2op	{"body":"Implemented in workspace bn-2op (commit 0e7a0f7). Added FrameSpec enum (Index(u8)|Rect(u8,u8)) and AnimDef.frames_rect: Option<(u8,u8)> in console-core/src/gfx_meta.rs. New single source of truth: AnimDef::resolve_frame(sprite, pos) composes frames_rect relocation + explicit tx:ty + the existing wrap-displacement math (wrap_frame_rect/explicit_frame_rect helpers); SpriteDef::frame_rect is unchanged (still backs non-anim dump/poke/edit addressing). Updated console-agent/src/sprite/view.rs's render_rect and anim_frames (the shared helper behind strip/onion/diff/ghost/gif/lint) to go through AnimDef::resolve_frame instead of SpriteDef::frame_rect directly -- one call site, so all anim-aware tools stay in sync automatically. lint's sprite_frame JSON field now serializes FrameSpec (plain number for Index, 'tx:ty' string for Rect). Grammar: anim ... frames=f0,f1,... fps=N [loop] [frames_rect=tx,ty], frames entries are i or tx:ty, mixable. Parse-time validation errors now name the anim and the 0-based frame-list position. Back-compat verified: all existing tests pass with only Vec<u8>->Vec<FrameSpec> call-site adjustments (no behavior change for classic anims). New tests: gfx_meta.rs unit tests (classic unchanged, frames_rect relocation, frames_rect wrap, explicit-ignores-frames_rect, off-sheet errors x2, bad-syntax errors x2, two-anims-one-sprite-disjoint-regions); new integration test crates/console-agent/tests/sprite_frames_rect.rs exercises render+strip+dump against a hand-built cart with markers at frames_rect-relocated tiles and an explicit tile, proving pixel-level correctness. SPEC.md and skills/build-cart/SKILL.md updated. cargo test --workspace green. No known overlap risk: gfx_meta.rs/sprite/view.rs untouched by other in-flight work per the task brief."}	blake3:HgAE3_doBqNB1_KvTnd_8n7cpVTA1kToWCowDvmbHVg
