1785730411721580	console-w-qw3	itc:v3:AWLM8yZ-TPM9AAAAAAAAQdva363t4AAAAAErBg		item.comment	bn-fcw	{"body":"Implemented in workspace bn-fcw (commit 4f3ee0d, branched from main pre-bn-2op). Added LintThresholds{max_drift,max_area_var,max_changed,no_unique_colors} + AnimSummary structs and lint_gated()/lint_summary() in console-agent/src/sprite/view.rs, both funneled through one new lint_anim_gated() (single source for the full-JSON report, the violations list, and the --summary numbers, so they can never disagree). Extracted PairMetrics/pair_metrics() out of the old inline pair_json() so unrounded drift/changed-pixel/area-drift values are shared between the report and the threshold checks. Added sprite_id ([tx,ty], the resolved sheet tile) to every frame JSON entry, unconditionally (not just under thresholds). lint(cart,names) keeps its exact old signature/behavior as a thin wrapper (LintThresholds::default()) -- all pre-existing lint tests pass unmodified, confirming 'no thresholds -> current behavior' back-compat. CLI: sprite lint gained --max-drift/--max-area-var/--max-changed/--no-unique-colors/--summary; run_view/cli_view now propagate a real exit code (0 default, 1 on any violation) instead of always 0 -- changed run_view's return type Result<(),String> to Result<i32,String>. RPC: sprite_lint mirrors the same threshold+summary params and returns a 'violated' boolean (JSON-RPC has no process exit code); violations/summary-anims keys only appear when thresholds are active or summary is requested, matching CLI shape. Violations name {anim,frame,metric,value,limit}; frame is the pair's 'to' frame (or the frame a unique color lives in); changed_pixels/area_drift_pct/centroid_drift gates are strictly-greater (equal to the limit does not violate). New tests: crates/console-agent/tests/sprite_lint_thresholds.rs (20 tests) covering pass/fail exit codes at the CLI level (cli_view direct calls, no subprocess), violations content/naming for all four metrics, --summary shape and its combination with thresholds, sprite_id correctness, and RPC-level threshold/summary/violated-flag behavior. IMPORTANT FOLLOW-UP: this workspace was created via 'maw ws create bn-fcw --from main', and main does not yet contain bn-2op (frames_rect=/explicit tx:ty anim frames) at the time of this work -- AnimDef.frames is still Vec<u8> here. sprite_id correctness is therefore only tested against the CLASSIC index-only frame form. Once bn-2op is merged, please add a follow-up test exercising sprite_id over a frames_rect=/explicit-tx:ty anim to confirm it reports the actually-resolved tile (not the naive sprite-rect-relative one) in the new forms too -- noted in the test file's header comment as well. SPEC.md and skills/build-cart/SKILL.md updated (lint flag list + CI quality-gate idiom). cargo test --workspace green (all pre-existing + 20 new tests)."}	blake3:e6Q1XhhXzQqdSKpwY7MTAA_wWkv-kcUuktiwB055ars
