1785731122620639	console-w-3sh	itc:v3:AWKTkkzJ8_JMklAAAAAAQa6ra-_VqoAAAAExAw		item.comment	bn-3sh	{"body":"Done, committed in ws bn-3sh (5dcdeef). `cargo test --workspace` green (27 suites), clippy clean.\n\nNew module crates/console-agent/src/music/ {mod,score,lint,roll,render}.rs, mirroring sprite/map.\n\nCLI:\n  music score      <cart> [--song N]\n  music lint       <cart> [--strict]\n  music piano-roll <cart> [--song N | --patterns a,b,c] [--cell N] [--row-h N] -o out.png\n  music render     <cart> [--song N] [--loops K=2 | --frames F] [--seed N] -o out.wav\n\nUX decisions:\n- Everything hangs off one shared SongPlan: the __music__ chain resolved from\n  --song N (music(N) semantics; defaults to the lowest pattern id), printed as\n  `pat 0 -> [pat 1 -> pat 2 ->] loop to 1` (ASCII arrows; bracketed span = the\n  loop body). Pattern length = max(rows*speed), the sequencer's own rule, so\n  intro/loop frame counts are exact.\n- The score grid's real axis is the FRAME, not the row: one line per frame at\n  which any slot starts a row, so mismatched slot speeds stay time-aligned.\n  The `row` column is filled in only when all slots share a speed (the common\n  case, where it is frame/speed); `:` = holding, `.` = sfx ended but still\n  claimed by music. Columns auto-sized so channels line up.\n- piano-roll x = frames (note length visible), y = semitone cropped to the used\n  range +/-2, one Sweetie-16 index per channel, brightness = velocity, octave\n  digits in a 6px gutter, loop bar in white.\n\nLint rules (all fired + not-fired in tests): env_sustain_swell,\nvib_delay_exceeds_row, note_out_of_range (note + sweep/arp/sl offsets off the\ntable), fm_aliasing (info, not a failure), wavetable_dc_offset (uses core's\ndc_sum), no_sfx_headroom (every pattern uses all 6), undefined_reference\n(error), unreachable_pattern, chain_has_no_terminator, pattern_clipping.\nNotes: (a) undefined sfx/pattern/instrument *inside* the cart data are already\nparse errors in core, so the useful version of that rule is music(n)/sfx(n)\nINTEGER LITERALS in __lua__ naming ids the cart lacks -- a real runtime halt the\nparser can't see. (b) unreachable_pattern derives song heads from those same\nliterals (falling back to in-degree-0 patterns, then the lowest id; reported as\nentry_source), and is suppressed when the cart calls music(<computed>) --\notherwise soundtest.cart flags 15 of its 16 patterns. (c) per-pattern peak comes\nfrom rendering each pattern alone on a synthetic cart built from the real\n__instruments__/__sfx__/__music__ text + `function _init() music(id) end`, so\nmaster/echo apply but the game's draw code doesn't.\n\nrender loop detection: static plan gives the frame budget; at runtime\nmusic_pattern() is sampled each frame and a \"pattern start\" is `id changed` OR\n`id unchanged and the pattern has run its full duration` -- the second half is\nwhat catches `pat 4 loop=4`, where the id never changes. Entry #K+1 into the\nloop-start pattern ends the render; music halting ends it immediately; ceiling\nis one spare loop pass. step() renders then advances, so the totals land exactly\non intro + K*loop (asserted for K=0..3, self-loop, stop, --frames).\n\nRPC: music_score{song?}, music_lint{}, music_piano_roll{path,song?,patterns?,\ncell?,row_h?}. Deliberately NO music_render verb -- in a session that is\neval{\"music(n)\"} + step + wav on the session's own console; flagged in SPEC.\n\nDocs: SPEC.md gets the harness subcommand/verb list + a full \"Inspection tools\n(music)\" section under Music authoring (replaces the phase-2 stub); SKILL.md's\nmusic layer list now leads with score/lint, then stats/events, then\npiano-roll/spectrogram/wav, plus checklist + serve-verb line.\n\nconsole-core untouched -- every accessor needed was already there\n(next_pattern_after, dc_sum, Fm::ratio_text, row_mod, instrument_at).\n\nMerge note: SPEC.md + SKILL.md are the only shared files (music sections only,\nplus one line each in the harness-verbs and serve-verbs lists); no overlap with\nthe sprite gfx_meta work."}	blake3:N2X3qGXj_xpNDbFfgXYUm7gVxu6p-F44cTsx-NguE48
1785731170400704	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEuaA		item.move	bn-3sh	{"state":"done"}	blake3:eyjJPAXz-0sJc7vcVkTKpfaK0awxxCwzfH3Q2VbLsg4
1785731840353654	console-w-2dq	itc:v3:AWLPmZmSTJP5NAAAAAAAQd9ttVq_rAAAAAEuAw		item.comment	bn-2dq	{"body":"aspr() landed in workspace bn-2dq (commit ac35c27) — NOT merged, lead merges.\n\nAPI (exactly three globals, console-core/src/api.rs):\n* aspr(name, x, y, [t0=0], [flip_x], [flip_y]) — plays a __gfx_meta__ anim.\n* anim_len(name) -> frame count.\n* anim_done(name, [t0=0]) -> true once a ONE-SHOT has held its last frame for its full 1/fps (raw step >= len); loops always false.\n\nDesign calls:\n* STATELESS: pos = floor((frame_count - t0) * fps / 60), rem_euclid(len) for loop, clamp(0, len-1) for one-shot. Integer, FLOORED (div_euclid) and saturating, so a t0 in the future steps backwards in even strides and no cart-supplied t0 can overflow. Zero new console state; determinism free.\n* (x, y) is the sprite's declared anchor=, NOT the top-left. spr() unchanged. The anchor does NOT mirror under flip — the dest rect is identical either way and flip only mirrors pixels inside it (so a character turning around stands on the same spot). Documented prominently in SPEC + SKILL.\n* Frame rects come from AnimDef::resolve_frame only; frames_rect= and explicit tx:ty frames work at runtime for free. New AnimDef::frame_at/done_at/step_at/len hold the playback maths (single source of truth shared by aspr and anim_done).\n* Blit goes through new gfx::spr_rect — the same private blit() spr()/map() use, pixel-addressed source. Camera/clip/pal/palt/fillp-exemption verified byte-identical to spr by test.\n* Unknown anim name = Lua error naming the typo AND listing the declared anims (or 'this cart has no __gfx_meta__ section'). Cart halts.\n* State gained one field: gfx_meta: Rc<GfxMeta>, read-only, never mutated.\n\nGOLDENS UNCHANGED — no re-record needed. Demo phases preserved EXACTLY: native fb hash for demo.cart/seed 0/120 frames of input 0 is still 0x5e743aea, and I rebuilt web/engine.js and ran node web/smoke.cjs: PASS, 0 failures, wasm fb 0x5e743aea + audio 0xbc2bd5e1f8c7f31e both unchanged. So native == wasm is already re-proven in this workspace.\n\nDemo cart: ANIM_* tables + anim_index/frame helpers + walk_t/idle_t counters all gone; star/gem/moth phase-lock (no t0), player walk/idle use two origins captured at the transition (t0 = f - 1, which is exactly what the old counters counted; comment explains). Reset (B) does walking, walk_t0 = true, f. Over the determinism script the new cart differs from the old ONLY at frames 72-79 (<=37 px), the third walk bout: walk now RESTARTS on its contact frame when you set off again instead of resuming a globally accumulated stride. Deliberate, nicer, and invisible to every golden (the golden run never moves).\n\nTests: 29 test binaries green, cargo clippy clean (the one remaining warning is pre-existing in console-agent/tests/sprite_frames_rect.rs, untouched).\n* new crates/console-core/tests/aspr.rs (16 tests): spr-parity frame-by-frame over two loops, anchor application (4 anchors incl. negative), all four flips, megatile + frames_rect + tx:ty, camera/clip/pal/palt/fillp parity, t0 restart equivalence, two origins in one frame, anim_len, anim_done timing per frame, one-shot holds last frame, unknown-name/sprite-name/no-section errors, halt stickiness, 50-instance replay determinism.\n* 6 new unit tests in gfx_meta.rs pin the fps mapping (8fps -> boundaries at 0/8/15/23/30), loop wrap, one-shot clamp, negative elapsed, saturation.\n* NEW native golden: tests/determinism.rs::demo_cart_framebuffer_matches_the_web_smoke_golden pins 0x5e743aea natively (smoke.cjs's twin did not exist before — the bone asked me to find it; it did not). Its doc comment documents the two-place re-record procedure.\n* tests/gfx_meta.rs::demo_cart_rendering_is_unaffected_by_gfx_meta had to change meaning: the section is load-bearing for the demo now, so it is replaced by demo_cart_without_gfx_meta_halts_naming_the_missing_anim. presence_of_gfx_meta_does_not_affect_rendering (non-aspr cart) still asserts back-compat.\n\nPerf: 50 aspr/frame over 60000 frames = 1.16 s (19 us/frame, ~0.39 us/call), identical within noise to the hand-rolled spr equivalent (1.11-1.24 s). demo.cart 20000 frames: 0.45-0.47 s before and after. ~0.1% of a 60fps frame budget for 50 sprites.\n\nDocs: SPEC.md gets three API-table rows, a new 'Declared animations: aspr, anim_len, anim_done' subsection (statelessness/t0 idiom + anchor semantics + error policy), the __gfx_meta__ heading/bullets updated (no longer 'runtime ignores it'), and aspr removed from Out of scope. SKILL.md's 'drive frames from your own Lua table' paragraph is replaced by a 'Playing anims at runtime: aspr' section with the walk/idle and one-shot-attack idioms, plus a note that manual tables remain right for exotic cases (non-uniform durations, ping-pong, velocity-driven speed). README one-liner updated.\n\nLead notes: web/engine.js IS rebuilt and committed in this workspace, so dist/ needs a repack after merge (dist/ is gitignored). demo.cart changed, so any packed game.html must be regenerated. I did NOT run a blanket cargo fmt — the local rustfmt is newer than the repo's formatting (same caveat cp0 flagged); I hand-matched rustfmt on my own hunks only, so the diff stays conflict-free."}	blake3:L56MSKlK6Lmgv51iQw8oQ6EEtcbloxeeZtuWUANQKHI
