1785733971588507	console-w-374	itc:v3:AWKcySSZzyZkmSRAAAAAQbtVW71tWqAAAAE0Aw		item.comment	bn-374	{"body":"Done, committed in workspace bn-374 (9313b27) - NOT merged.\n\n## music edit - six verbs, CLI only, --dry-run everywhere\ntranspose [sfx-ids] [semis] [--clamp] | copy [src] [dst] [--force] | shift-rows [sfx-id] [n] | set-vol [sfx-id] [0-7 | +n | -n] | set-inst [sfx-id] [voice] [--where old] | stretch [sfx-id] [2 | 0.5] [--force]\n\nUX decisions:\n- Own arg parser (EditArgs): a leading '-' is an OPERAND, not a flag, so `transpose 0 -12` works. Only `--` prefixes are treated as flags.\n- transpose takes an id, a range `0-5`, or a list `0,2,5-7`; the other five take one id (a range there gets a bespoke error saying only transpose takes a set).\n- Range errors compute the fit: \"sfx 0 row 0: C4 -60 leaves the note table (C0-B7); the selection fits any shift in -48..=+40 - nearest to -60 is -48\". --clamp clamps instead.\n- set-vol preserves rests (scaling silence into a note would be wrong); a signed prefix means relative, a bare 0-7 means absolute.\n- set-inst validates the voice against the cart (wave digit / w-slot / instrument name) and --where matches the exact spelling `music score` prints.\n- stretch rounding is DOCUMENTED and PRINTED: doubling uses max(1, ceil(speed/2)) (speed 5 becomes 3), halving uses speed*2; when the legal 1..=255 range blocks it the speed is left alone and the summary says so. Every run prints the old/new frame count plus the delta, so nothing is silent. speed=auto is resolved to a number and a loop= range is rescaled with the rows.\n- copy/stretch/shift-rows move ORIGINAL row text; transpose/set-vol/set-inst do token surgery in which the following whitespace run absorbs the width change, so hand-aligned grids stay aligned and fx columns ride along untouched.\n\n## music import-abc\n`music import-abc CART TUNE.abc --sfx N [--inst] [--vol] [--speed] [--transpose] [--force] [--dry-run]` (a bare - reads the tune from stdin)\n- Hand-rolled parser, no new dependencies. Rational Frac durations throughout (with Add/Mul/Sub impls).\n- 1 row = gcd of the note lengths, not \"shortest note\" (which breaks on mixed 2- and 3-unit lengths). A held note is a repeated row: sample-identical to a sustain on a flat voice, re-attacks on env/sweep, and the report says so. That also makes splitting at the 32-row cap free and exact.\n- Supported: X/T/M/L/Q/K/V fields plus inline [K:], octave marks, sharps/flats/doubles/naturals, key signatures including all seven modes, bar-local accidentals, z/x/Z rests, a2 a/ a/2 a3/2 lengths, ties (merged into one row run), broken rhythm, bar lines (validated against M:, warn-only), repeats and endings (played once, with a warning), chords (first note kept, with a warning), grace notes / decorations / annotations dropped. Tuplets and voice overlays are rejected BY NAME rather than mis-imported.\n- Out-of-range notes error with the ABC token named and the nearest fitting --transpose computed.\n- Output: notes/rests, key/meter/L, the row grid and speed with their derivation, sfx ids, split points, a suggested bpm=/rows_per_beat= header and one `pat` line per sfx.\n\nFixture tunes (inline in tests/music_abc.rs): a D major scale exercise; The Butterfly (trad. Irish slip jig, 9/8, Em, a repeat and a tie across a bar line); a 16ths etude (explicit accidentals in both directions, a rest, a broken rhythm); Ode to Joy (dotted-eighth/sixteenth figure). Pitches pinned note by note.\n\n## Files\nNEW: crates/console-agent/src/music/{sfxtext,transform,abc}.rs and crates/console-agent/tests/{music_edit,music_abc}.rs\nMOD: crates/console-agent/src/music/mod.rs (modules, dispatch, usage); crates/console-agent/src/rpc.rs (comment recording that there is no music_edit/music_import_abc verb because cart mutation is CLI-only, placed next to the existing map_poke note); SPEC.md (two new phase-3 sections plus the subcommand list); skills/build-cart/SKILL.md (\"Score-level editing\" and \"ABC import\" blocks with the import/score/edit/lint/render workflow, the RPC note and the checklist).\nconsole-core: UNTOUCHED (0 files).\n\n## Status\ncargo test --workspace green (32 suites; 48 new tests: 25 in music_edit, 23 in music_abc, plus lib unit tests). cargo fmt --check clean. clippy clean except one pre-existing warning in tests/sprite_frames_rect.rs that predates this bone.\n\n## Merge notes\nThe only shared files are SPEC.md and SKILL.md. The SPEC edits are two appended sections just before \"Out of scope\" plus one line in the subcommand list; the SKILL edits are two appended subsections just before \"### Wavetables\" plus three small in-place edits. Neither should collide with the console-core audio worker (periodic noise / tremolo). If that bone adds a wave id or an fx token, transform.rs's validate_voice caps bare digits at 5 (mirroring the parser) and would want the same bump; abc.rs only ever passes the --inst value through, so it needs nothing."}	blake3:69erXm6qTT-Fxl-Pl-gzIkpRTbQCpEz7P0O_xckUaAQ
