1785734367572621	console-w-1i7	itc:v3:AWKSeZmT8_nJQAAAAAAAQavba_f3UAAAAAEsAw		item.comment	bn-1i7	{"body":"Done, committed in ws bn-1i7 (65d2529). cargo test --workspace green (all suites incl. new lint_trem_delay_exceeds_row), cargo fmt clean on touched files.\n\nAdded trem_delay_exceeds_row beside vib_delay_exceeds_row in crates/console-agent/src/music/lint.rs: fires when an instrument's trem delay >= the sfx's row length (speed frames), same severity (warn), same message shape and JSON fields (sfx/row/delay/row_frames/instrument). Since trem is instrument-only (no Fx column spelling, per SPEC.md), the check only reads inst.trem -- no 'row fx' branch like vib has. Row length reused exactly as vib does: u32::from(sfx.speed).\n\nAdded fired/not-fired test pair lint_trem_delay_exceeds_row in crates/console-agent/tests/music.rs, mirroring lint_vib_delay_exceeds_row's structure (same delay=12/speed=8 fires, speed=16 quiet).\n\nDocs: SPEC.md's music-lint rule list gets a trem_delay_exceeds_row bullet after vib_delay_exceeds_row; skills/build-cart/SKILL.md's 'music lint catches mechanically' list now says 'vibrato and tremolo that never speak' instead of just vibrato.\n\nNote: cargo fmt --all also reformatted an unrelated pre-existing line in crates/console-agent/src/music/transform.rs (validate_voice's wave-digit error message) -- reverted that hunk manually so this commit stays scoped to the trem rule."}	blake3:hMxYeIy-ZQE7Z-gFCkj-RSi6C2khi2PloCuEWKBPRho
