1785867247494442	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEu6AI		item.comment	bn-3pt	{"body":"Art bible drafted and strict visual-judge PASS after one blocking revision. Contract now specifies reference-derived hierarchy, upper-right lighting with flip-safe actor exception, exact Apollo ramps, cluster rules, 10 live frog poses plus 6 mutation/pickup overlays, 92x58 boss assembly matching live envelopes, rotationally neutral VFX, exact runtime sockets, stable terrain IDs/classes, and an identity-palette migration. Atlas allocation independently verified: 90+6+36+40+18+24+16+20+6=256 with no overlap/gap. Full just check passes."}	blake3:rkzviESFf6yHtdtsHgWIbKiocmovwuK7ERganXf0cwI
1785867835883249	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEu6QI		item.update	bn-3le	{"field":"description","value":"# Context and background\nThe strict judge scored frog craft 4.6 out of 10. The visible frog is a static-eyed procedural oval whose thin limbs disappear, while declared frog sprites are not used by the player render path.\n\n# Goal\nCreate and render a distinctive authored frog atlas with anatomical clarity, expressive poses, visible momentum, and persistent mutation silhouettes.\n\n# Implementation approach\nFollow carts/ribbit-recoil-art/ART-BIBLE.md and the PNG bridge. Author exactly ten 24x24 full frames at the allocated origins: idle; run A/B; rise; fall; swing tuck/extend; laser brace; fire breath; hurt. Author the six allocated 8x8 overlays for blink, victory expression, persistent Laser Eyes, persistent Fire Breath throat/back, and the two pickup icons. Do not add hop compression unless the runtime first gains a visible anticipation state and the atlas budget is revised. Victory reuses rise plus its overlay. Replace draw_frog_pose in gameplay, title, and victory with sprite-backed composition, using identity palette scope during the legacy transition.\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n- Gameplay no longer uses the procedural frog renderer.\n- Major live actions have distinct body mechanics, not merely relocated line limbs.\n- Grounded motion uses run A/B; vertical velocity selects rise/fall; swing selects tuck/extend by tension/speed.\n- Laser and fire alter silhouette in action and remain identifiable through overlays in ordinary movement.\n- Blink and victory use the allocated overlays; no unbudgeted compression or full victory frame is introduced.\n- Mouth, eye, feet, anchor, and 14x16 physics box match the art-bible socket table.\n- Sprite strip/onion/GIF/lint and runtime sequence evidence pass.\n- Hitboxes and deterministic traversal remain unchanged or receive explicit regressions.\n- Native 1x readability and packed browser presentation are inspected.\n\n# Project value\nFixes the always-visible asset that currently creates the largest reference-quality gap."}	blake3:Q8M4oM4VCw7pEHGaTyHtbru35SW3CuRCjX5XYg2xHe0
