1786047451928930	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEuzwQ		item.create	bn-7za	{"description":"A full 192x320 `console run --screen-text` dump produces hundreds of very wide lines and overwhelms agent logs. Add bounded diagnostic modes for selecting a framebuffer region and obtaining a compact summary while preserving exact full-frame output when explicitly requested. Design a machine-readable contract for coordinates, dimensions, palette/glyph counts, non-background bounds, truncation metadata, and invalid bounds. Add CLI help, JSON/text coverage, output-budget tests, and build-cart skill guidance showing agents how to inspect HUDs, dialogs, and small collision areas without dumping the entire display.","kind":"task","size":"m","title":"Add bounded regions and summaries to screen-text diagnostics"}	blake3:INNlW2-LXwYcOAHi3OgftA8-NnNppzwRjMmGXJt-1QM
1786047452105402	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEu0AQ		item.create	bn-2ov	{"description":"Build on bn-1wv's bounded `ecs_query` inspector. Let agent tooling define named, bounded ECS queries once and sample them across selected frames without resending selectors or scraping unrelated state. Results should report stable query metadata plus useful deltas such as alive/matched/returned changes, spawned/despawned entity IDs within strict caps, component-count changes, truncation, and sampling frame. Specify replay/reset behavior, pagination coherence, memory/output budgets, protected registry access, native/WASM parity, RPC and CLI integration, and documentation. Include tests observing a Radiant Swarm enemy wave, bullet growth, and nova clear across frames.","kind":"task","size":"l","title":"Add saved ECS watch queries and frame-to-frame deltas"}	blake3:-aeM_Oa5iLJEajpCBm3yyEo4XJiSI8wUaNWMV5thxBM
1786047452275113	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEu0QQ		item.create	bn-rt0	{"description":"Radiant Swarm uses ad hoc globals such as `dev_status`, `dev_start`, `dev_stress`, and `dev_damage_boss`. Define a small optional convention or manifest-declared registry for named development hooks that playtests, `console run`, and agents can discover and invoke deterministically. Hooks need descriptions, bounded scalar/table arguments and results, explicit lifecycle phase, sandboxing, duplicate/name validation, replay/reset semantics, and production behavior. Integrate with declarative playtests, expose discovery through agent RPC/CLI, document recommended status/start/stress/damage patterns, and migrate Radiant Swarm as the reference cart.","kind":"task","size":"l","title":"Standardize deterministic cart development and stress hooks"}	blake3:F5NHkv9Ac2RILJPNV6g9XB2oywPgTWZE0iVhYH6v_2w
1786047452455009	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEu0gQ		item.create	bn-b7f	{"description":"Give examples/radiant-swarm a focused game-design and audiovisual polish pass while preserving its ECS stress role. Add more recognizable enemy formations, attack patterns with readable setup-development-release sentences, stronger boss phase transitions and telegraphs, and clearer rewards for grazing and pickups. Improve nova, damage, phase-change, and pickup audiovisual feedback without obscuring bullets or overwhelming the mix. Retune encounter pacing from title through victory, add controlled variation without breaking seeded determinism, update automated playtest assertions/artifacts, and verify readability at the existing 250+ entity storm density.","kind":"task","size":"l","title":"Polish Radiant Swarm encounter language and combat feedback"}	blake3:z6uJJc5PyZujMHzGA45XNGh2ovyKsncF4I6zw3lYUnw
